tly, and do not create your own subclasses of this class. The shape","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"classes correspond to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Geometry","type":"text"},{"text":" object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types in the GeoJSON standard, but some have nonstandard names for backwards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compatibility.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Although you do not create instances of this class directly, you can use its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape\/shapeWithData:encoding:error:","type":"reference"},{"text":" factory method to create one of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"concrete subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape","type":"reference"},{"text":" noted above from GeoJSON data. To access a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shape’s attributes, use the corresponding ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNFeature","type":"reference"},{"text":" class instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can add shapes to the map by adding them to an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","type":"reference"},{"text":" object.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Configure the appearance of an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","type":"reference"},{"text":"’s or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","type":"reference"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shapes collectively using a concrete instance of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Alternatively, you can add some kinds of shapes directly to a map view as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"annotations or overlays.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can filter the features in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer","type":"reference"},{"text":" or vary their layout or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paint attributes based on the features’ geographies. Pass an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape","type":"reference"},{"text":" into an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPredicate"},{"text":" with the format ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SELF IN %@"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"%@ CONTAINS SELF"},{"text":" and set the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer\/predicate","type":"reference"},{"text":" property to that predicate, or set a layout or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paint attribute to a similarly formatted ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSExpression"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolyline":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolyline","fragments":[{"text":"MLNPolyline","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/